    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1781">

                <pb facs="1162" n="1046" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg1046"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 819.74/56.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Price to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Panama</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-08-14">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 14, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your instructions August 13 complied with. Panaman Minister for Foreign Affairs
                    agreed this morning that the United States <pb facs="1163" n="1047"
                        xml:id="pg1047"/> should take complete control of wireless telegraph
                    situation in both the Republic of Panama and its territorial waters. I at once
                    notified Governor Goethals and he notified Lieut. Crenshaw, who has taken charge
                    of the situation.</p>
                <p>Panaman President then issued a decree carrying out said agreement.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Price</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
